::: {.bio}
My research brings together political theory, data science and statistical methods. I'm particularly interested in how we measure political beliefs, and what those measurements can tell us. Currently, I'm investigating how we evaluate large language models using established political psychology scales. Alongside my research, I act, sing and write songs, and I produce art films, music, commercials and narrative films.

## Biography

[For programmes, press and introductions]{.label}

Delphine PA Dang is a Vietnamese artist, musician and researcher in Sydney. She approaches art and creative work through her close relationship with data science and statistics, and with international relations, political theory and political thought. Her intellectual focus spans political theory, computational international relations and psychometrics, and her artistic practice is strongly research-oriented: her art film *An Eye for an I* turns her findings on large language models into an audiovisual work.

Beyond her primary creative pursuits, Delphine practises acting, composing and singing. In collaboration, she takes on the roles of producer, composer-vocalist, assistant director and strategic manager to realise the visions of artists and brands. She edited the music video *Be My East* (dir. Gavin Goh), which won Best Cinematography at the Sony Catchlight Festival 2026.

Delphine trained in opera singing for seven years, an undertaking that began after she won the Golden Buzzer on *Vietnam's Got Talent*, the moment that marked the start of her professional vocal training. Alongside opera, she plays bass and has a background in ballet, theatre and acting. These performative disciplines inform her wider artistic sensibility, shaping how she approaches composition, presence and narrative across her visual and research-driven work.
